Biological diagram/infographic showing a human body with organ callouts and estimated cell counts by tissue or category. Labels include Peripheral Retina 1.20M, Heart 0.68M, Liver 0.44M, Blood 4.18M, Kidney 0.35M, Brain 7.48M, Lung 1.20M, Breast 2.25M, Others 6.46M, and Pan-Cancer 2.68M. Each callout includes a representative cell type description, such as neuron, pericyte, hepatocyte, B cell, podocyte, pulmonary alveolus, myoepithelial cell, basal cell, and plasma cell.

No axes or plotted quantitative trends are shown. The main visible content is a body-map summary of biomedical tissue/cell categories and their associated counts, likely from a single-cell or cell atlas resource.
